09744_013681_rtc"},{"date":"2026-10-29","platform":"sentinel-1c","relativeOrbit":21,"orbitState":"descending","meanDb":-11.02,"stdDb":5.51,"validFraction":1.0,"deltaDb":-0.11,"changeFlag":false,"precipMm":2.6,"item":"S1C_IW_GRDH_1SDV_20261029T033552_20261029T033617_010094_014261_rtc"},{"date":"2026-11-10","platform":"sentinel-1c","relativeOrbit":21,"orbitState":"descending","meanDb":-11.11,"stdDb":5.53,"validFraction":1.0,"deltaDb":-0.09,"changeFlag":false,"precipMm":0.0,"item":"S1C_IW_GRDH_1SDV_20261110T033551_20261110T033616_010269_01481F_rtc"}],"lastPairChangedFraction":0.0068,"method":"Sentinel-1 RTC gamma0 VV (terrain-flattened), relative orbit 21 (descending) only, to keep the illumination geometry. 2400 m window centered on the site (240×240 px at 10 m, azimuthal equidistant projection, nearest neighbor). One scene per fortnight (the first with ≥90 % valid pixels) over the last 365 days; the last two are consecutive passes of the same orbit. meanDb/stdDb = mean and standard deviation of 10·log10(gamma0). deltaDb = meanDb(t) − meanDb(t−1). changeFlag = |Δ| > 1.5 dB, or |Δ| > 2σ_Δ with |Δ| ≥ 0.5 dB (robust σ_Δ = 1.4826·MAD of the site's Δ). lastPairChangedFraction = fraction of pixels with |Δ| > 3 dB between the last two scenes after a 5×5 (50 m) mean filter in linear power to reduce speckle. precipMm = accumulated daily precipitation of the scene day and the 2 previous days (UTC), Open-Meteo Archive (reanalysis, ~0.1°–0.25° cell); null if unavailable.","interpretation":"Between 2025-11-20 and 2026-11-10 the mean gamma0 VV in the window ranged from -11.2 to -9.9 dB (range 1.3 dB). 2 change(s) flagged: 2026-03-20 (Δ +0.9 dB, 16.8 mm in 72 h — coincident with precipitation); 2026-04-01 (Δ -1.3 dB, 2.1 mm in 72 h — coincident with precipitation). All are below 1.5 dB: statistical anomalies relative to the site's own variability, on the order of Sentinel-1 radiometric uncertainty (~0.5–1 dB). Backscatter increases coincident with precipitation are consistent with a possible increase in surface moisture, without proving the cause. The change of 2026-04-01 reverses the previous one: possible return to the previous level (e.g. drying), i.e. a transient episode rather than a persistent change. Between the last two passes, 0.7 % of the pixels (filtered to 50 m) changed by more than 3 dB.","license":"CC BY 4.0 (Sentinel-1 RTC, Planetary Computer)","credit":"Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2025–2026","source":"https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/dataset/sentinel-1-rtc","notes":["Orbit used: relative 21 (descending), VV polarization; 70 acquisitions of that orbit in the period, 24 selected. Other orbits present: 87 ascending (61).","Robust site σ_Δ = 0.07 dB; flagged scenes: 2 of 23 pairs.","Fraction of pixels with |Δ| > 3 dB in the last unfiltered pair: 0.089 (speckle-dominated; the published value uses the 5×5 filter).","A backscatter change can be due to soil moisture (rain/dew), sand migration or remobilization, snow/ice or frost, ephemeral vegetation or residual geometry/calibration differences; this product does not attribute causes.","Reanalysis precipitation is a cell-scale estimate (tens of km) and may not reflect local rain."]}
